hey guys it's jenna here in my previous  video i shared some of my results from  my genetic tests i did with circle dna  in this video i'm going to dive in a  little deeper to find the right diet for  your body type if you have been eating  well and exercising regularly yet you're  not getting the results you're looking  for perhaps you are still unknowingly  doing the wrong thing for your body type  some of you might have even tried all  the diets out there low fat low carbs  high fat high protein but nothing seems  to work and you just don't know what to  do  not every diet suits everyone if you  want to see effective results the diet  you choose needs to be optimal according  to your genetics so based on my circle  dna results my optimal diet is healthy  balance there are four categories in  this section depending on your results  you might fall under low carb low fat  mediterranean or healthy balance so how  do we determine this  if you look under fat sensitivity and  carb sensitivity both my results are  normal this means my body isn't highly  sensitive if i were to consume cups or  fats in my diet hence i fall under  healthy balance because i can't consume  them in moderation if however your  results show that you have a higher  sensitivity towards carbs but a normal  fat sensitivity then the optimal diet  type for you will be low carb on the  other hand  if you have a higher sensitivity towards  fat and a normal cup sensitivity then  the optimal diet type for you will be  low fat  if  your results show that you have a higher  sensitivity towards both carbs and fats  then the optimal diet type for you will  be mediterranean so based on your  results how do you then cook and eat  according to the diet recommended to you  before i share the meal suggestions if  you haven't yet done your dna test and  you're curious about your body type go  to circledna.com to find out more about  the different services they offer you  can use the coupon code joanna at  checkout to get one kit for 35 off two  to three kids for 40 off and four or  more kids for 50 off  this is applicable to any circle dna kit  you purchase and this offer is only  limited to the first 100 kids sold so do  share this information with your family  and friends let's take a look at the  four diet types and the meal suggestions  let's start with my optimal diet which  is healthy balance if you fall under  this category you are lucky because your  body tolerates fats and carbs well hence  the recommendation is to consume  everything in moderation your healthy  plate should look like this  half vegetables quarter protein and  quarter cups fill your plate with a  variety of colorful vegetables as they  are a great source of vitamins minerals  antioxidants and dietary fiber you can  also add a piece of fruit into your meal  as for protein go for high quality  proteins such as chicken fish meat  tempeh tofu beans legumes and yogurt the  general recommendation is about 0.8  grams of protein per kilo of your body  weight but if you are active then you  should be consuming between 1.2 to 1.7  grams of protein per kilo of your body  weight for example i'm 50 kilos and  because i'm active i would consume about  1.5 grams of protein per kilo of my body  weight that means i should eat about 75  grams of protein a day how i would  achieve that is to consume 2 eggs for  breakfast one portion of salmon for  lunch and  one portion of white fish for dinner  that gives me a total of 72 grams of  protein  you need enough protein to perform  strength training and to build lean  muscle mass  based on my nutrition report i have a  higher need for iodine omega-3 dha  vitamin b12 and vitamin b6 hence i  follow a pescetarian diet and will  consume oily fish such as salmon tuna or  mackerel at least three to four times a  week if you are a vegetarian or vegan  you can also consider taking supplements  if you find meeting your daily  requirements from food alone is  difficult as for carbohydrates choose  healthy complex cups such as rice quinoa  oats buckwheat noodles sweet potatoes  pumpkin whole grain pasta or wholemeal  bread i have been following a healthy  balanced diet for several years now and  i have seen great results i have enough  strength and energy for my training and  i've also improved my body composition  by reducing my body fat and increased my  total lean muscle mass let's have a look  at the low carb diet if you fall under  this category that means you have a  higher sensitivity towards cups and your  body has a high resistance to insulin  insulin is the hormone responsible for  controlling your blood sugar levels a  high level of insulin resistance means  that your blood sugar levels are likely  to spike after consuming cups especially  refined cups  some of the common signs of cup  sensitivity include an intense craving  for refined cup foods such as sweets  bread pasta biscuits cereals and cake  struggle with never really feeling full  which can lead to overeating energy  level tends to dip after an hour of  consuming cups  they tend to gain weight easily and they  experience carbohydrate withdrawals such  as headaches irritability mood swings  and anxiety  carb sensitivity is a real thing and it  might be the reason why weight loss can  be challenging for those who fall under  this category this doesn't mean that you  cannot consume carbs at all but you need  to choose the good cups and limit the  portion so if this is you here's how you  can make adjustments to your meals  first thing is to eliminate all refined  cups in your diet only go for healthy  complex cups such as quinoa oats  buckwheat brown rice sweet potatoes  pumpkin and beans next  limit your cup intake to about 100 to  150 grams per day here's an example of  how to portion our cups in your meals  half a cup of oats for breakfast  one small bowl of cooked brown rice for  lunch and around 150 grams of sweet  potatoes for dinner including the  vegetables you add into your meals  you're told total cup intake for the day  will be about 110 to 150 grams of cups  to feel satisfied and reduce your  cravings you can increase your protein  and non-starchy vegetable intake when  you're cup sensitive consuming carb rich  foods has a greater impact on your  overall well-being than merely reducing  your calorie intake so you have to pay  more attention to the types of carbs you  consume  if your optimal diet is low fat then  following a high fat or keto diet just  won't work for you having a higher  sensitivity towards fat does not mean  you cannot consume fats in your diet the  importance with a low fat diet is to  differentiate between the types of fats  since fat sensitivity is specifically  linked to saturated fats so you will  want to limit the amount of saturated  fats and choose unsaturated fats instead  saturated fats are found in animal  products such as red meat skin of  poultry full-fat dairy products eggs  cheese cream butter ghee lot and even  tropical oils such as coconut oil and  palm oil consuming too much of saturated  fats can increase ldl the bad  cholesterol levels unsaturated fats are  considered heart healthy they are  typically found in plant foods such as  avocados olives nuts and seeds as well  as fatty fish such as salmon mackerel  and tuna consuming more unsaturated fats  can help to reduce ldl levels and  increase hdl for good cholesterol  typically a low fat diet follows a  higher carb more protein and low fat  thai plan this means that 55 to 60 of  your calories can be from cups  20 from protein and the remaining 20 to  25 from fats  in general following a predominantly  plant-based diet would be suitable for  you  without making it too complicated here  are few simple guidelines to follow in  reducing your saturated fat intake trim  off any visible fat from meats and  remove skin from poultry before cooking  consume more plant-based foods which are  rich in protein and cups such as beans  peas lentils tempeh and tofu avoid  deep fried foods  choose healthier cooking methods such as  baking roasting steaming boiling or  poaching  avoid fatty and processed meats such as  bacon sausage ribs and luncheon meats  if you want to eat red meat then limit  it to only two to three servings per  week and choose leaner cuts  and the final diet type is mediterranean  if you have a higher sensitivity towards  both carbs and fats then this would be  the recommended diet for you as it is  low in cups low in saturated fats and  higher in unsaturated fats  i visited greece several years ago and  stayed there for a month i absolutely  love their way of eating i love the  flavors and it was really wholesome and  satisfying someone who follows a  mediterranean diet typically consumes a  wide variety of vegetables whole grains  fish seafood olive oil nuts seeds  legumes and potatoes  they would consume poultry eggs cheese  and yogurt in moderation and rarely  consume red meat they limit their  consumption of soft drinks processed  meats or refined grains  olive oil is the primary source of added  fat in the mediterranean diet they would  use it in their cooking instead of using  butter they would also substitute red  meat for seafood poultry or beans they  do also enjoy a variety of cheese in  small quantity and plain yogurt the  mediterranean diet is a delicious and  healthy way to eat  this diet is also suitable for me as it  meets my higher needs for oily fish once  again it's important to recognize that  our body type is not a life sentence  your body type will shift based on your  lifestyle activity and diet  modifications by understanding your  genetics you will be able to make the  right diet choice suitable to you rather  than blindly following a diet trend out  there do you know what's the optimal  diet for you let me know in the comments  below to find out more about your body  type go to circledna.com and key in the  coupon code joanna to get up to 50 off  links are in my description box below if  you enjoyed this video and find the  information to be extremely useful then  do share it with your family and friends  in my next video we will discover more  about the right type of exercise you  should be doing according to your body  type so be sure to stay tuned and do  also subscribe to my youtube channel for  a lot more workout videos nutritional  tips and fitness tips all the best
 

